  "The music table, the contract with the engine: written by the composer's table.py (and render.py) from audio/music/tracks/*.json and bible/moods.json. Do not edit; edit those.",
  "tracks.<name>: class (a loudness class in audio.json music.classes), tempo, bars, beats_per_bar, seconds (the loop's exact length; every stem is this long), dir (the stems' folder in the engine), layers in order: id, state (`base` always plays; any other is raised by the engine), db (the level baked into the stem), file.",
  "moods.<mood>: track (which track the mood plays) and states (the states the engine may raise while this mood plays; a state with no layer in the track does nothing there).",
  "states.<state>: how the engine raises it, in prose; the code is the engine's.",
  "silence_db: the volume a stem is faded to when its state is off; 0 dB is on."
